      "owner": "frontend",
      "severity": "high",
      "blocking": true,
      "summary": "AC 24 (UX-5-1) says \"every control in the form that takes keyboard focus (reached by Tab from the first box through to Save and the decisions and follow-up controls)\". The phone test (`frontend/e2e/retrospective.spec.ts` ~L416-441) checks only \"What didn't\" (focus), \"Lessons for next projects\", Tunde Bello, Ada Obi and \"Add a decision\". It never checks \"What went well\", the Reference field, the Notes file select, the decision fields, the follow-up controls, or Save. The criterion's own check is therefore not met as written, and a regression on those controls would pass. Expected: a Tab walk from the first box to the last control (or a loop over all focusable controls in `form` that excludes the bar's own controls), with the same bottom-above-bar and `elementFromPoint` assertions for each. Actual: five sampled controls. Path: `frontend/e2e/retrospective.spec.ts:416-441`.",
      "reproduction": null,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "delivery/features/F-119B/round-1/review-technical.md"
      ],
      "raised_by": "reviewer-technical",
      "state": "FIX_SUBMITTED",
      "history": [
