      "owner": "frontend",
      "severity": "low",
      "blocking": false,
      "summary": "`clearOfBar` (`RetroForm.tsx`, the `requestAnimationFrame` in the focus handler) is not cancelled when the form unmounts or the focus moves again. The callback reads `bar.current` and calls `window.scrollBy` after the component may have gone, which is harmless today but can scroll a page the user has left. Expected: keep the frame id and `cancelAnimationFrame` it in an effect cleanup, or accept as a known trade-off. Path: `frontend/src/features/retrospective/RetroForm.tsx` (`clearOfBar`).",
      "reproduction": null,
